<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32153" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōchus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὦχος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Bactriana</i>, <i>that
				empties into the Oxus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 16,
				18, § 49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 7,
				10, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 6,
			57</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A surname of Artaxerxes III.</i>, <i>king of Persia</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 10, 5,
			23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Son of Darius Codomannus</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 4,
				14, 22</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>